# ============================================================
#  Places (design §6.1). Positions are on the campus map
#  (960 × 680, see docs/map-concept.svg): the castle stands on the
#  north shore of the Mirror Lake, the village to the south-east,
#  the Whisperwood to the west. Data only until phase 2b.
#
#  open:      the slots a place can be visited in
#  discover:  when it becomes visible (omit for places open from the start)
#  hint:      teaser shown while hinted (hinted_when) but not yet discovered
#  draws:     tags of older events (no place: yet) that may happen here (compat, phase 2b)
# ============================================================

# ---------------- Public from the start ----------------

@place courtyard
name: The Courtyard
region: castle
map: campus 585,278
kind: public
open: morning noon afternoon evening night
art: tower
draws: social festival rival story
desc: Flagstones worn smooth by three centuries of students, a fountain that freezes when it shouldn't, and the best gossip in the castle.

@place library
name: The Library
region: castle
map: campus 380,275
kind: public
track: library_assistant
open: morning noon afternoon evening night
art: book
draws: study
# The revision card comes first on a term visit, once a term (2026-10-19).
always: library_revision
desc: Seven floors of shelves that rearrange themselves when nobody is looking. Footnote the cat keeps order.

@place refectory
name: The Refectory
region: castle
map: campus 470,278
kind: public
open: morning noon afternoon evening midnight
art: meal
draws: social home money
desc: Long tables, longer benches, and soup that tastes faintly of whatever you're homesick for.

@place lakeshore
name: The Lakeshore
region: grounds
map: campus 480,505
kind: public
open: morning noon afternoon evening night midnight
art: wave
draws: nature mystery romance
desc: The Mirror Lake lies so still it shows the towers upside down. On some nights it shows other things.

@place village
name: The Village Square
region: village
map: campus 720,520
kind: public
open: morning noon afternoon evening
art: house
draws: money home
# The shop counter (world expansion 1, K3): what it sells, first on every visit.
always: shop_square
desc: A barge ride across the lake: crooked roofs, a market square, a bakery that has fed students for two hundred years and shopkeepers who have seen every kind of student.

# ---------------- Castle ----------------

@place lecture_tower
name: The Lecture Tower
region: castle
map: campus 420,180
kind: public
open: morning noon afternoon evening
art: scroll
draws: class study exam
desc: Spiral lecture halls stacked one above another. Evocation on the lower floors, where scorch marks are expected; Umbral Theory at the top, where the lamps burn dim.

@place observatory
name: The Observatory
region: castle
map: campus 600,175
kind: public
open: afternoon evening night midnight
art: planet
draws: magic mystery
desc: A brass dome at the top of the east tower. The great telescope points wherever it likes; usually that is the right place.

@place great_hall
name: The Great Hall
region: castle
map: campus 455,215
kind: public
open: noon afternoon evening
art: crown
draws: festival social
desc: Floating candles, a vaulted ceiling that shows tomorrow's weather, and the stage where the choir rehearses and the Midwinter Ball is held.

@place infirmary
name: The Infirmary
region: castle
map: campus 530,200
kind: public
open: morning noon afternoon evening night midnight
art: potion
draws: crisis danger
desc: Clean white beds, a cupboard of tonics and Sister Amaranth, who has seen every kind of injury and believes none of the excuses.

@place alchemy_lab
name: The Alchemy Laboratory
region: castle
map: campus 555,240
kind: public
open: morning afternoon evening
art: cauldron
draws: class magic
desc: Long benches, cauldrons in every size, and a ventilation charm that has given up on the third floor.

@place workshop
name: Mir's Workshop
region: castle
map: campus 615,235
kind: public
open: afternoon evening night
closed_when: flag(mir_workshop_shut) and since(mir_workshop_closed) < 3
discover: met(mir)
hint: Something clanks and hums behind the west-wing tapestry.
hinted_when: turn >= 2
art: gear
draws: magic
desc: A former classroom full of springs, gears, half-finished machines and the smell of solder. Fire buckets by the door, on the faculty's orders.

@place job_board
name: The Job Board
region: castle
map: campus 520,262
kind: public
open: morning noon afternoon evening
art: paper
draws: job money
# The job menu first on every visit, then one odd gig (feedback 2026-10-15).
always: job_board_visit
desc: A cork board in the entrance hall layered with notices: jobs, lost familiars, club recruitment and the occasional ransom note for a sock.

@place ledger_office
name: The Lumen Ledger Office
region: castle
map: campus 395,230
kind: club
track: lumen_ledger
open: afternoon evening night
discover: member(lumen_ledger) or met(nessa)
art: paper
draws: club
desc: A cramped room under the library stairs, walls papered with old front pages. The printing press groans like a dragon on deadline night.

@place headmistress_tower
name: The Headmistress's Tower
region: castle
map: campus 500,130
kind: public
open: afternoon evening
discover: rel(isolde) >= 12 or flag(warden_trial)
hint: A spiral stair guarded by a stone owl that only opens its eyes for some students.
hinted_when: met(isolde)
art: crown
draws: story
desc: Books, tea and a board of crystal towers by the window. You are only here because she wants you here.

@place restricted_section
name: The Restricted Section
region: castle
map: campus 352,245
kind: public
open: afternoon evening midnight
discover: flag(forbidden_key) or seen(forbidden_section_1) > 0 or flag(heist_stacks_known)
hint: A door at the back of the library that is always locked, and always slightly warm.
hinted_when: turn >= 2
art: lock
draws: mystery danger
desc: Black-bound books that breathe in the dark. Some of them read you back.

@place gargoyle_passage
name: The Third Gargoyle
region: castle
map: campus 418,135
kind: society
track: cartographers
open: afternoon evening midnight
discover: member(cartographers)
hint: Corvin keeps glancing at a particular gargoyle.
hinted_when: met(corvin)
art: map
draws: club mystery
desc: Behind the third gargoyle on the north parapet, a passage that isn't on any map. Except theirs.

@place night_market
name: The Night Market
region: village
map: campus 885,575
kind: public
open: midnight
closed_when: not term
discover: flag(night_market_known)
hint: The village says there's something in the far field after midnight, when there's no moon.
hinted_when: turn >= 3
art: lantern
always: night_market_stalls
draws: money mystery
desc: A field past the last stile, full of hooded stalls and coloured flames on the moonless night of every term month, and empty grass by dawn.

@place seventh_tower
name: The Seventh Tower
region: castle
map: campus 500,72
kind: public
open: afternoon evening midnight
discover: clue(lead_seventh_tower) or clues(hollowstar) >= 4 or flag(heist_tower_known)
hint: A locked stair that leads up into a tower nobody admits is there.
hinted_when: clock(hollowstar) >= 1
art: key
draws: mystery story
desc: Locked for a century. At the very top, one room of dust and moonlight, and a star-shaped hollow in the wall.

@place thesis_lab
name: The Thesis Laboratory
region: castle
map: campus 565,160
kind: thesis
track: thesis
open: morning afternoon evening
discover: year >= 4
art: book
draws: study
desc: Rows of carrels where final-year students and their advisors argue about footnotes until the candles give out.

# ---------------- Grounds ----------------

@place duel_hall
name: The Duelling Hall
region: grounds
map: campus 660,150
kind: club
track: duelling
open: afternoon evening
discover: member(duelling) or rel(lyra) >= 9
hint: Steel rings somewhere above the east stair.
hinted_when: met(lyra)
art: duel
draws: rival
desc: Scorched floorboards and a ceiling that has seen things. The practice dummies have names, and grudges.

@place greenhouses
name: The Greenhouses
region: grounds
map: campus 740,235
kind: club
track: verdant
open: morning afternoon evening
discover: member(verdant) or met(tobias) or met(maud)
art: leaf
draws: nature
desc: Glass houses that steam even in winter. The moonflowers bloom once every eleven years; the mandrakes have opinions every day.

@place flight_field
name: The Flight Field
region: grounds
map: campus 850,300
kind: public
open: morning afternoon evening
art: broom
draws: club
desc: A long green field with hoops at either end and a wind that cheats. Broom lessons, races and spectacular landings.

@place stables
name: The Familiar Stables
region: grounds
map: campus 845,385
kind: public
open: morning afternoon evening
art: paw
draws: nature
desc: Hippogriffs, a sulky griffon chick, owls in the rafters and Professor Brask, who talks to all of them more kindly than to students.

@place boathouse
name: The Boathouse
region: grounds
map: campus 610,440
kind: public
open: afternoon evening night midnight
art: wave
draws: social mystery romance
# A boathouse night (feedback 2026-10-16): the ring first (either door), then one drawn card.
always: midnight_boathouse_ring|ring_on_yourself
desc: An old wooden boathouse and a jetty out over the water. People come here to say the things they can't say indoors.

@place orchard
deprecated: maud_cottage
name: The Orchard
region: grounds
map: campus 790,165
kind: public
open: morning noon afternoon evening
art: tree
draws: nature romance
desc: Apple and pear trees older than the towers. In spring the blossom falls like snow; once, it was snow.

@place maud_cottage
name: Old Maud's Cottage
region: grounds
map: campus 780,400
kind: public
open: morning noon afternoon evening
discover: met(maud)
art: house
draws: nature home romance
desc: A thatched cottage with chickens on the doorstep, bees in the eaves, a goat called Bartholomew and a kettle that is always nearly boiling. Behind it, apple and pear trees older than the towers.

@place secret_garden
name: The Secret Garden
region: grounds
map: campus 815,425
kind: public
open: morning afternoon evening
discover: seen(garden_maud_secret) > 0
hint: A door in the wall behind the potting shed that you keep walking past.
hinted_when: met(maud)
art: flower
draws: nature magic
desc: Glowing ferns, silver bees and a pear tree that hums. It only exists for people Maud has shown it to.

@place courier_loft
name: The Courier Loft
region: grounds
map: campus 880,230
kind: job
track: broom_courier
open: morning afternoon evening
discover: turn >= 3
art: letter
draws: job
desc: A draughty loft full of parcels, pigeonholes and brooms in various states of repair. The dispatch bell rings at all hours.

# ---------------- Village ----------------

@place gilded_newt
name: The Gilded Newt
region: village
map: campus 800,480
kind: job
track: tavern
open: afternoon evening night midnight
art: cup
draws: job money social
# A Newt night (feedback 2026-10-16): the company offer first, then the high table.
always: newt_company newt_company_regular newt_high_table shop_newt
desc: The village tavern: low beams, a fire that never goes out, and a landlady who remembers every student's tab to the penny.

@place mabels
name: Mabel's Tea Shop
region: village
map: campus 725,565
kind: public
open: morning noon afternoon evening
art: cup
draws: social home
# The shop counter (world expansion 1, K3): what it sells, first on every visit.
always: shop_mabels
desc: Forty kinds of tea, three kinds of cake and Mabel, who reads your mood from the way you open the door.

@place grimsbys_books
name: Grimsby's Books
region: village
map: campus 680,600
kind: public
open: noon afternoon evening
art: book
draws: study money
# The shop counter (world expansion 1, K3): what it sells, first on every visit.
always: shop_grimsbys
desc: A bookshop so crowded the shelves lean on each other for support. Mr Grimsby will find anything except what you came in for.

@place pell_apothecary
name: Pell & Daughters
region: village
map: campus 770,600
kind: job
track: apothecary_clerk
open: morning afternoon evening
art: bottle
draws: job money
# The shop counter (world expansion 1, K3): what it sells, first on every visit.
always: shop_pell
desc: An apothecary of a thousand labelled drawers. Old Pell taught three generations to count drops; his daughters taught him to smile at customers.

@place bakery
deprecated: village
name: The Bakery
region: village
map: campus 640,555
kind: public
open: morning noon afternoon
art: meal
draws: home money
desc: The same family has baked here for two hundred years. The buns are famous; so, in certain circles, is a letter that arrived very late.

# ---------------- Wilds ----------------

@place whisperwood
name: The Whisperwood
region: wilds
map: campus 185,340
kind: public
open: morning afternoon evening night midnight
discover: met(maud) or flag(fox_met)
hint: Fog sits on the western woods even at noon.
hinted_when: turn >= 2
art: tree
draws: nature danger mystery
always: ww_edge ww_edge_night|ww_night_first
desc: An old forest that talks in its sleep. Moonpetal grows in its clearings; so do things that are better left there.

# ---------------- Internship hosts (design §7.5) ----------------
# Six hosts sit on the two break maps (new maps, 2026-11-10; below): an intern's map is the whole capital or
# countryside. Thornwick keeps a map of its own (the rival school, across the hills).

@place thornwick_lab
name: The Thornwick Exchange Lab
region: internship:thornwick
map: thornwick 480,300
kind: internship
track: intern_thornwick
open: morning afternoon evening
art: mask
desc: A guest laboratory at Thornwick Academy, the rival school, where the illusionists are excellent and the hospitality is suspicious.

# ---------------- The capital (map: city; new maps, 2026-11-10) ----------------
# The river runs from the uptown towers through midtown's bridges to Port Calder's docks. A noble, a merchant or a
# street origin goes home here; anyone may travel here on a break; four internship hosts are here. Homes and the
# Conclave and the Office are found only by the people they belong to.

@place royal_library_archives
name: The Royal Library
region: capital
map: city 235,150
kind: internship
track: intern_royal_library
open: morning noon afternoon
art: book
desc: Miles of stacks beneath the capital, where the oldest records of the realm are kept in temperature-controlled silence. Upstairs, a reading room anyone may use, if they whisper.

@place conclave_laboratory
name: The Conclave Laboratory
region: capital
map: city 125,105
kind: internship
track: intern_conclave
discover: member(intern_conclave)
closed_when: not member(intern_conclave)
open: morning afternoon evening
art: wand
desc: The research laboratory of the Conclave of the Seven Towers, where new spells are tested behind very thick walls.

@place unseen_office
name: The Office of Unseen Affairs
region: capital
map: city 330,95
kind: internship
track: intern_unseen_office
discover: member(intern_unseen_office)
closed_when: not member(intern_unseen_office)
open: evening night
art: eye
desc: The Crown's Office of Unseen Affairs. It has no sign, no address, and a very good coffee machine.

@place capital_townhouse
name: The Family Townhouse
region: capital
map: city 420,165
home: has(origin_noble)
kind: plan
discover: has(origin_noble)
open: morning noon afternoon evening night
art: house
draws: home social
desc: Your family's house uptown: the best beds in the capital, a cook who remembers what you like, and dinners where every word is noticed.

@place capital_club
name: The Members' Club
region: capital
map: city 530,120
open: afternoon evening night
art: cup
draws: social money
desc: Leather chairs, low voices and a porter who decides who you are. Patrons, collectors and other people's parents come here to be seen not being seen.

@place capital_bazaar
name: The Grand Bazaar
region: capital
map: city 445,300
open: morning noon afternoon evening
art: coin
always: shop_bazaar
draws: money social
desc: A covered market the size of a cathedral: spices, charms, maps, instruments, and a hundred things nobody at home has heard of.

@place capital_arcade
name: The Arcade of Services
region: capital
map: city 305,355
open: morning noon afternoon evening
art: scroll
always: shop_arcade
draws: money
desc: A colonnade of brass plates and open doors: physicians, tutors, scribes, a bathhouse, a portraitist and a fortune-teller who takes appointments.

@place capital_theatre
name: The Theatre
region: capital
map: city 600,265
open: afternoon evening night
art: mask
draws: social
desc: The capital's great theatre, gilt and draughty. Its boxes see more of each other than of the stage.

@place alchemists_works
name: The Guild Works
region: capital
map: city 185,430
kind: internship
track: intern_alchemists
open: morning noon afternoon
art: cauldron
desc: The Guild of Alchemists' great works by the river: vats, chimneys and a strict rule about naked flames. The hiring hall by the gate takes on hands for the day.

@place capital_docks
name: The Docks
region: capital
map: city 710,535
open: morning noon afternoon evening night
art: wave
draws: money danger social
desc: Port Calder's wharves, where the river meets the sea: barges, cranes, gulls and men who can lift a crate and a purse in one movement.

@place capital_counting_house
name: The Counting House
region: capital
map: city 615,600
home: has(origin_merchant)
kind: plan
discover: has(origin_merchant)
open: morning noon afternoon evening night
art: coin
draws: home money
desc: The family firm's house on the wharf: ledgers below, beds above, and a clerk who has been there longer than the door.

@place capital_crew_loft
name: The Crew's Loft
region: capital
map: city 845,425
home: has(origin_street)
kind: plan
discover: has(origin_street)
open: morning noon afternoon evening night
art: house
draws: home danger
desc: A loft above a chandler's in the old streets of Port Calder: hammocks, a stove, and people who knew you before you had a wand.

# ---------------- The capital, round 2 (2026-11-11; docs/maps-plan.md): the peers' homes and the busy streets ----------------
# A peer's home is found once you've met them, and they're there when you visit the capital on a break (their
# `schedule_break:` names it beside their castle places).

@place vaneshade_house
name: Vaneshade House
region: capital
map: city 456,88
discover: met(lyra)
open: noon afternoon evening
art: crown
desc: Black stone on the Crescent, a black seal over the door, and a footman who looks at your boots first. Lyra lives here, in a manner of speaking.

@place oracle_rooms
name: The Oracle's Rooms
region: capital
map: city 656,82
discover: met(seraphine)
open: noon afternoon
art: eye
desc: Where the Oracle of Vell sits for the court in season: a hushed upper floor, a queue of anxious people in good coats, and Seraphine in a window seat.

@place hollis_house
name: Hollis House
region: capital
map: city 725,128
discover: met(bram)
open: noon afternoon evening
art: house
desc: A narrow, very correct house on the uptown side, with a polished plate on the door and a father inside who was once head boy.

@place capital_gardens
name: The Royal Gardens
region: capital
map: city 805,212
open: morning noon afternoon
art: flower
desc: Gravel walks, a fountain, hothouses full of things that shouldn't grow this far north, and everyone uptown walking slowly to be seen.

@place capital_cathedral
name: The Cathedral of the Lamp
region: capital
map: city 345,238
open: morning noon afternoon evening
art: candle
desc: A spire you can see from the sea, a lamp that has burned for four hundred years, bells that tell the whole city the time, and a crypt of archives under it all.

@place capital_printing_row
name: Printing Row
region: capital
map: city 548,382
open: morning noon afternoon evening
art: paper
desc: A street of presses, ink and shouting, where the capital's broadsheets are set by hand and anything said by noon is news by dusk.

@place capital_bridges
name: The Lamplighters' Bridges
region: capital
map: city 486,440
open: afternoon evening night
art: lantern
desc: The three old bridges, crowded with buskers, hawkers and couples, and lit every dusk by the lamplighters' guild one lamp at a time.

@place ten_clockworks
name: The Ten Clockworks
region: capital
map: city 96,520
discover: met(mir)
open: noon afternoon evening
art: gear
desc: A workshop and a house in one, among the works chimneys: forty clocks all ticking, a family at the long bench, and Mir's old room above the shop.

@place capital_coaching_yard
name: The Coaching Yard
region: capital
map: city 328,560
open: morning noon afternoon evening night
art: map
desc: Where the coaches come in from the countryside and the north: horses, porters, travellers with all their luggage, and people who make a living off travellers.

@place capital_fish_market
name: The Fish Market
region: capital
map: city 641,492
open: morning noon afternoon
art: wave
always: shop_fish_market
desc: On the quay from dawn: barrows, gulls, shouting, the night's catch on ice, and the best gossip in Port Calder before it's breakfast anywhere else.

@place ashby_lane
name: Ashby Lane
region: capital
map: city 762,470
discover: met(corvin)
open: morning noon afternoon evening night
art: door
desc: A crooked lane in Port Calder where the houses lean together and everyone knows the Ashbys. Corvin doesn't talk about it. Now you know why, or will.

@place capital_undercroft
name: The Undercroft
region: capital
map: city 528,478
discover: flag(undercroft_known)
hint: Dockers talk about somewhere under the middle bridge where the dice never stop.
hinted_when: visits_to(capital_bridges) + visits_to(capital_docks) >= 1
open: evening night
art: dice
draws: money danger
desc: The old cellars under the middle bridge, where the river drips through the vaults: dice, cards, a pit with sawdust on the floor, and people who buy things without asking where they came from.

@place capital_rookery
name: The Rookery
region: capital
map: city 893,368
discover: has(origin_street) or flag(rookery_known)
hint: In Port Calder, people look up at the roofs a lot.
hinted_when: visits_to(capital_docks) + visits_to(ashby_lane) >= 1
open: evening night
art: raven
draws: danger
desc: The rooftops of Port Calder, where the houses lean so close you can cross a street without touching it: chimney-pots, washing lines, the crews' old routes and the whole city spread out below.

@place capital_tide_caves
name: The Tide Caves
region: capital
map: city 904,590
discover: has(origin_street) or flag(tide_caves_known)
hint: On the docks, old men talk about the sea's back door.
hinted_when: visits_to(capital_docks) >= 1
open: noon afternoon
art: wave
draws: nature danger mystery
desc: Under the headland past Port Calder's breakwater, the sea has hollowed the rock into caves that open only at low water: the smugglers' old road, and the sea's door at the far end.

@place capital_crescent_house
name: The House on the Crescent
region: capital
map: city 520,58
discover: flag(crescent_known)
hint: At the club and under the bridge, people talk about a shipowner's safe.
hinted_when: visits_to(capital_club) + visits_to(capital_undercroft) >= 1
open: evening night
art: mask
draws: social danger
desc: The tallest house on the Crescent, uptown, where a shipowner who bought his way up the hill gives a ball every week he's in town: lit from cellar to attic, the mews door open for the trays, and a safe in the study the size of a wardrobe.

@place capital_bonded_warehouses
name: The Bonded Warehouses
region: capital
map: city 765,612
discover: has(origin_street) or flag(bonded_known) or flag(tide_bonded_drain) or flag(crew_job_done)
hint: On the docks, people talk about the bonded warehouses the way sailors talk about reefs.
hinted_when: visits_to(capital_docks) >= 1
open: night
art: lock
draws: money danger
desc: The customs' warehouses on Port Calder's wharf, where goods wait under the crown's seal until their duty is paid: a glass-topped wall, yard dogs, a watchman's round and the richest floor in the city.

# ---------------- The countryside (map: home; new maps, 2026-11-10) ----------------
# Two villages on one road through fen, moor and ridge. A scholar or a hedge origin goes home here; anyone may travel
# here on a break; two internship hosts are here. Everything looks fine.

@place home_market
name: The Market Village
always: market_inn_hands shop_country_market
region: countryside
map: home 615,300
kind: plan
open: morning noon afternoon evening
art: coin
draws: money social
desc: A green, a market cross and the coaching inn where the road changes horses. Everyone is very glad to see you.

@place countryside_mill
name: The Mill Village
always: mill_miller_sacks
region: countryside
map: home 300,385
open: morning noon afternoon evening
art: wave
draws: mystery social
desc: A huddle of cottages round a mill and a small grey chapel. The wheel turns slowly, and the children sing at their skipping.

@place home_cottage
name: The Family Cottage
region: countryside
map: home 382,470
home: has(origin_scholar)
kind: plan
discover: has(origin_scholar)
open: morning noon afternoon evening night
art: house
draws: home
desc: The kitchen table, the creaky stair, the smell of whatever is in the oven. Everyone asks how school is.

@place countryside_marsh
name: The Marsh
region: countryside
map: home 170,545
home: has(origin_hedge)
open: morning noon afternoon evening night
art: leaf
always: shop_hedge_door
draws: nature mystery
desc: Reed beds and black water where the river gives up. Lights move out there at dusk. A hedge-witch keeps a house on stilts at the edge.

@place home_fields
name: The Fields
always: fields_harvest_day
region: countryside
map: home 490,200
kind: plan
open: morning afternoon evening
art: leaf
draws: nature
desc: Long rows of good harvest under a big sky, and scarecrows in very decent coats.

@place countryside_moors
name: The Moors
region: countryside
map: home 775,250
open: morning noon afternoon evening
art: paw
draws: nature danger mystery
desc: Heather, cairns and bog roads, and a fog that comes up from nowhere. The shepherds don't go out past the third cairn.

@place field_station
name: The Beastcraft Field Station
region: countryside
map: home 870,175
kind: internship
track: intern_field_station
discover: member(intern_field_station)
closed_when: not member(intern_field_station)
open: morning afternoon evening
art: paw
desc: A cabin on the moors, ringed with paddocks and nesting towers, where injured creatures are mended and wild ones are counted.

@place countryside_ridge
name: The Ridge
region: countryside
map: home 705,95
open: morning afternoon evening night
art: planet
draws: nature mystery
desc: A long bare ridge above the villages, with a ring of standing stones and a view of every star there is.

@place observatory_camp
name: The Expedition Camp
region: countryside
map: home 585,105
kind: internship
track: intern_expedition
discover: member(intern_expedition)
closed_when: not member(intern_expedition)
